@@ -2,6 +2,14 @@
 
 ## Player / trailer preview
 
+### Correct short-media completion without accepting stale EOS
+
+The native duration-tail check can mark a clip of one second or less complete at position zero after its video queue drains, before its first position callback. This is a confirmed source-level path; it has not been established as the cause of an observed device failure.
+
+Simply requiring native end-of-stream (EOS) is not a complete correction. Early EOS is currently ignored before the first position callback, and a clock can stop at the last video sample below the container duration. The physical playback epoch also survives an in-place seek, so it does not distinguish delayed pre-seek EOS from the new segment's completion. Removing the position guard or requiring the full duration alone is insufficient.
+
+A correction must exercise the real queue/pump and callback ingress: short-duration boundaries, EOS before the first position, synchronous EOS submission, retired epochs, seek before/after EOS, missing EOS with a clamped clock, and audio extending beyond video. Preserve the existing exact-seek and failed-producer guards. A passing host check does not establish native device completion behavior.
+
 ### Grade `hero_scrim_a`'s legibility contract against synopsis text over live trailer video
 
 **What:** Add a row to `widgets::hero_scrim_a`'s anchor table for "synopsis-weight (`LABEL` 26px)
