+update. On reopening, check those actual choices, Favorites and the saved
+interface mode. Do not reload a stale Home export over newer settings just to
+make the screen resemble an earlier installation. For Classic selection and
+Back behavior, see [Classic navigation](classic-list-settings.md#choose-classic-and-navigate-back).
+
+Reuse the existing OTT controller pairing and verify an authenticated reconnect
+with the expected Device ID. An update is not a reason to register a new device
+or generate a replacement token. Matching file metadata alone does not prove
+that all saved values or the protected pairing token were successfully loaded.
+
+### Verify the build that is actually running
+
+Close the previous application normally, install the verified package in place,
+and launch **OTTPlay** normally. Match the installed application ID, version and
+executable hashes to the package. Then obtain a fresh OS running-process result
+and foreground result after launch: the foreground application must be
+`com.openottplay.player.native`. A live native PID can be behind another app;
+neither that PID nor a launch acknowledgement proves that OTTPlay is visible.
+If foreground cannot be read, record that verification as incomplete.
+An installed-file hash is not a hash of a running process's mapped executable;
+record that limitation when firmware prevents reading the latter.
+
+The latest local diagnostic installation recorded here, on **2026-11-04**,
+used native source `5a90b06658e08a526343d0d39ff4ee512923e554` and OTTPlay
+integration source `ed6cf394f54ce1cbb796fbf3c36ef5248e7ff151`, with numeric version **0.3.0**.
+The 28,444,804-byte IPK had SHA-256
+`688744979ee8e8244750c7c15cb4378e971ea8ee5d176b26fc0621353290f445`;
+the installed main executable matched
+`096266ec2d841add0104bd2f80648b1c3532f0317f9074d27f702b061efeb00c`.
+
+This replaced the earlier `f21d4688` build in place. All three installed
+executables matched the package; storage and companion were unchanged.
+One installation and one normal launch completed, and a fresh OS query after
+launch confirmed `com.openottplay.player.native` in the foreground. The fixed
+set of saved-state file metadata remained unchanged; no old settings snapshot
+was restored. The temporary package was removed.
+
+This record describes a local diagnostic build. It does not establish a public
+release, catalogue or playback acceptance, successful protected-state reload,
+or rollback compatibility. Saved-state contents were not read by the installer,
+and the live process's mapped executable was not hashed.
+
+### Plan rollback separately
+
+Retain the previous verified package, its source identity and the recovery
+material supported by that version's storage scheme. Before reinstalling an
+older package, check both the platform's version policy and whether the older
+code can read the current saved data. Do not assume that a successful forward
+update proves downgrade compatibility, or uninstall to force a downgrade.
+The installation above did not test rollback. After any approved rollback,
+repeat the installed-build, fresh process/foreground and configuration checks;
+never overwrite newer preferences or pairing with an old snapshot blindly.
+
