index e87cb811..a249f31c 100644
--- a/docs/webos5-port.md
+++ b/docs/webos5-port.md
@@ -482,3 +482,26 @@ This is the single most useful contribution available to this project.
 
 Even "it starts and the UI works but the video is black" is a decisive result — it separates
 §4.1 from everything else in one report.
+
+
+### Host simulator: decoded exact-seek preroll
+
+The optional Mac screenshot decoder now distinguishes the decode keyframe from the requested
+presentation position. `VideoSink::seek_with_target` leaves the native LG implementation at its
+existing keyframe boundary. Only an armed host picture decoder opts into an exact presentation
+floor: it receives all compressed reference frames, discards decoded pictures before the target,
+and publishes the first eligible picture before starting its presentation clock. Clock-only host
+runs keep the same keyframe semantics as before. This is not evidence of exact seeking on LG.
+
+The host exact-seek generation owns its picture and readiness together. Replacement seeks and
+teardown retire old decoder output. Its input queue is bounded; waiting for the first eligible
+picture expires after 15 seconds. Clean decoder EOF, successful writer completion, an empty pending timestamp queue, and
+successful process termination are needed to report an empty tail; truncation or decoder failure is a failure, not a successful seek. An
+empty paused seek stays paused until the viewer resumes. The ordinary native EOF/prime policy is
+unchanged, and ordinary best-effort screenshot playback does not opt into this exact-seek policy.
+
+Qualification requires host unit checks plus a real Mac decoder run with a sparse-GOP file:
+forward/backward seek, paused seek, replacement while preroll is pending, and a short/empty tail.
+Tests of the policy and injected decoded output do not prove FFmpeg pixel output. The physical LG
+sink still needs its own verified decode-start/presentation-start contract before exact clipping
+can be enabled there.
